      "writtenOn": "2026-09-17T02:41:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Understood on the D-Bus object. My concern is what the skip leaves behind.\n\n  Skipping an offset holds the last published state. Once the health state set\n  lands, a component sensor whose op_state read ENABLED with a non-critical\n  health state, and which later reports op_state FAILED, keeps `Functional`\n  true, so Redfish Health stays OK for a sensor that has stopped reporting.\n\n  On the log volume: I tested on a CX7 and op_state stayed at the same value\n  across many polls, so a log gated on a change from that offset\u0027s previous\n  op_state would not flood the journal. A log does not stop a consumer from\n  reading the stale value, but it does let someone debugging see that the\n  sensor stopped reporting, which nothing shows today. Worth having either way.\n\nThanks",
